### **Option 2: Create a systemd service (recommended)**

1. Create the service file:

```bash
sudo tee /etc/systemd/system/kea-dhcp4.service <<'EOF'
[Unit]
Description=Kea DHCPv4 Server
After=network.target

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/kea-dhcp4 -c /usr/local/etc/kea/kea-dhcp4.conf
Restart=on-failure

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
EOF
```

2. Enable and start the service:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now kea-dhcp4
```

3. Check status:

```bash
systemctl status kea-dhcp4
```

* You should see the service **active (running)**.

